# Which files here are *documents* to be typeset, as opposed to libraries that
# a document \inputs. One name per line; blank lines and # comments ignored.
#
# Explicit rather than inferred, because every rule anyone proposed for telling
# the two apart was wrong on this directory: plipsum.tex has no \bye and neither
# does story.tex; pliptest.tex has both \input and \bye and story.tex has
# neither. A manifest cannot drift silently the way a heuristic can.
#
# tools/done_check.sh wraps each with `\input plain` / `\bye` when the file does
# not supply them itself, and requires the run to set the same characters, in
# the same order, as `tex -ini` on the same source.
story.tex
pliptest.tex
